# T-205 — MONTHLY, on the 15th, closing the month that ended a fortnight earlier. The job is
# idempotent per period (verified at source, not assumed: `runDepreciation` no-ops an
# already-posted period with `created: false`, and amortisation reads `postedPeriods` and skips via
# `already.has(period)`), so a second run in the same month writes nothing.
#
# ⚠️ 02:00 Manila is the same window as recurring-expense-draft (02:00) and ahead of
# order-wastage-backstop (02:30) — but those are 1st-of-month units and this one is the 15th, so
# they never contend. `shareat-month-end-retry.timer` fires the SAME service again at 03:00 as the
# retry Ian asked for; on a successful 02:00 run it finds everything posted and does nothing.
#
# ⛔ THE ZONE IS LOAD-BEARING AND ITS ABSENCE WAS THE ORIGINAL DEFECT (DEF-241). Until 2026-09-10
# this line read `OnCalendar=*-*-01 02:00:00` with NO zone, and systemd reads an unzoned OnCalendar
# as UTC — so month-end ran 02:00 UTC = **10:00 Manila**, mid-working-day, while every sibling that
# cares about wall-clock time pinned Asia/Manila deliberately. Never remove `Asia/Manila`.
#
# ⛔⛔ AND THE FIX FOR DEF-241 INTRODUCED A WORSE, SILENT ONE — THIS IS WHY THE DATE MOVED (DEF-283).
# `lastCompletedPeriod()` (`packages/domain/src/scheduler/index.ts:196`) derives the period from
# **UTC**: it takes `getUTCMonth()` and returns the month before it. Pinning the run to 03:00
# Asia/Manila **on the 1st** puts the firing instant at 19:00 UTC on the LAST DAY OF THE PREVIOUS
# MONTH — so `getUTCMonth()` still reads the outgoing month and the job would have closed the month
# BEFORE the one that just ended. Executed, not reasoned: firing for February 2027 at 03:00 Manila
# on 1 March = 2027-02-28T19:00Z, and `lastCompletedPeriod` returns **2027-01**. February would
# never have been closed by cron at all — DEF-044's shape exactly, the silent non-execution this
# whole job exists to prevent.
# ⭐ It never bit because `docs/ops` does not deploy (DEF-194) and the corrected file was never
# installed. The bug was live in git and dead on the droplet.
# ⭐ **The 15th is immune by construction**, and that is a reason to keep it beyond Ian's own: it
# sits ~8 hours clear of any month boundary, so the UTC/Manila skew cannot change which month
# `getUTCMonth()` reports. ⛔ **Do not move this back near the 1st or the 31st without fixing
# `lastCompletedPeriod()` to be zone-aware first.**
#
# ⭐ Ian's ruling, 2026-09-10: *"it must be run every 15th of the next month at 2 am and 3am if 2am
# fails"* — superseding his own 03:00-on-the-1st call earlier the same day.

[Unit]
Description=Shareat — month-end close, monthly on the 15th (closes the previous month)

[Timer]
OnCalendar=*-*-15 02:00:00 Asia/Manila
# ⚠️ Catch up after a reboot or an outage rather than skipping silently. A month-end that quietly
# skipped because the box was down is DEF-044's shape all over again — that defect was exactly this
# job (v1's depreciation cron) going silent for two months, found by an audit, not a person.
Persistent=true
AccuracySec=5min

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
